1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,337
Many websites start from a static HTML template.

2
00:00:04,337 --> 00:00:08,107
This video turns one into a working Orchard Core theme:

3
00:00:08,107 --> 00:00:13,608
you copy the assets, declare the resources, build the layout, template the content,

4
00:00:13,608 --> 00:00:15,400
and add a setup recipe.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,881
A static template is a finished design:

6
00:00:22,881 --> 00:00:27,810
HTML pages, a stylesheet, scripts, and images, filled with sample text.

7
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:32,740
The goal is to keep the design and let Orchard Core supply the content.

8
00:00:33,490 --> 00:00:36,075
The built-in TheBlogTheme was created this way.

9
00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:39,490
It is a port of the Clean Blog template from Start Bootstrap, so

10
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:42,660
its source code is a real reference while you follow along.

11
00:00:43,410 --> 00:00:48,204
You need an Orchard Core CMS application, an empty theme project in your

12
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:52,507
solution, and the template with its CSS, JavaScript, and images.

13
00:00:52,507 --> 00:00:55,580
In the examples, the theme is named MyTheme.

14
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:59,379
Four tasks turn the template into a theme:

15
00:00:59,379 --> 00:01:04,334
copy the assets, declare them as resources, convert the main page into a

16
00:01:04,334 --> 00:01:08,464
layout, and convert the inner pages into content templates.

17
00:01:08,464 --> 00:01:10,560
A setup recipe is optional.

18
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:20,244
Copy the template's stylesheet, scripts, images, and icon into the wwwroot folder of

19
00:01:20,244 --> 00:01:23,230
the theme project, as this file tree shows.

20
00:01:23,980 --> 00:01:31,849
The static file middleware serves everything in wwwroot under the name of the theme project.

21
00:01:31,849 --> 00:01:40,200
So css/styles.css is available at /MyTheme/css/styles.css, which is the address the resources use.

22
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:50,339
Instead of hardcoded link and script tags, you register the template's stylesheets and

23
00:01:50,339 --> 00:01:52,469
scripts as named resources.

24
00:01:52,469 --> 00:01:59,570
Orchard Core then handles version hashes, minified and debug files, CDN addresses, and dependency order.

25
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:06,018
A class that implements IConfigureOptions of ResourceManagementOptions declares them.

26
00:02:06,018 --> 00:02:11,715
DefineStyle and DefineScript give each resource a name, and SetUrl takes the minified

27
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:14,220
file first, then the readable one.

28
00:02:14,970 --> 00:02:19,767
Register the class in the Startup class of the theme with AddResourceConfiguration.

29
00:02:19,767 --> 00:02:22,840
The theme can then ask for these resources by name.

30
00:02:23,590 --> 00:02:28,028
When the template depends on a library such as Bootstrap, define the library

31
00:02:28,028 --> 00:02:31,546
as a resource of its own, and list it with SetDependencies.

32
00:02:31,546 --> 00:02:35,010
TheBlogTheme does this, so the library always loads first.

33
00:02:39,210 --> 00:02:42,909
The layout is the markup that every page shares.

34
00:02:42,909 --> 00:02:50,239
Copy the template's main page, usually index.html, to a file named Layout.liquid in the Views folder.

35
00:02:50,239 --> 00:02:53,870
Keep its markup, and replace what is hardcoded.

36
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:59,091
Replace the hardcoded link and script tags with the resources you declared.

37
00:02:59,091 --> 00:03:02,900
The style tag and the script tag take the name of the resource,

38
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:05,660
and the script goes to the foot of the page.

39
00:03:06,410 --> 00:03:07,958
Keep the resources tags.

40
00:03:07,958 --> 00:03:12,343
They render the stylesheets, scripts, and meta tags that other modules and your

41
00:03:12,343 --> 00:03:16,367
own templates register at runtime, so the layout needs them even when it

42
00:03:16,367 --> 00:03:18,070
does not use them directly.

43
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:24,786
Replace the hardcoded page content with render_body, and the static navigation list with the menu shape.

44
00:03:24,786 --> 00:03:29,070
The shape renders the content items of the menu that has the given alias.

45
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:35,852
Add render_section wherever widgets should be able to appear, such as the header and the footer.

46
00:03:35,852 --> 00:03:40,760
With required set to false, a page that puts nothing in a zone still renders.

47
00:03:41,510 --> 00:03:44,424
A Razor layout follows the same pattern.

48
00:03:44,424 --> 00:03:50,822
RenderBodyAsync and RenderSectionAsync replace the Liquid tags, and the style, script, and menu

49
00:03:50,822 --> 00:03:54,180
tag helpers replace the resource and menu tags.

50
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:58,678
The menu shape renders its items as a list.

51
00:03:58,678 --> 00:04:03,705
If the navigation of the template needs specific CSS classes, override the Menu

52
00:04:03,705 --> 00:04:08,850
and MenuItem templates in the Views folder, plus a MenuItemLink template for each

53
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:11,570
type of menu item, as TheBlogTheme does.

54
00:04:15,837 --> 00:04:20,524
The layout renders zones, and the admin offers widgets only in the zones

55
00:04:20,524 --> 00:04:22,087
that the site lists.

56
00:04:22,087 --> 00:04:26,834
In the admin, Settings, Zones has the field Available zones for Layers, a

57
00:04:26,834 --> 00:04:29,297
comma separated list of zone names.

58
00:04:29,751 --> 00:04:33,081
Design, Widgets shows one card for each listed zone.

59
00:04:33,081 --> 00:04:37,618
Content is the zone that render_body renders, and the Footer zone holds a

60
00:04:37,618 --> 00:04:40,891
widget that the layout renders with render_section.

61
00:04:41,390 --> 00:04:45,204
On the front end, that widget appears at the bottom of the page,

62
00:04:45,204 --> 00:04:49,290
because the layout renders the Footer zone inside its footer element.

63
00:04:53,490 --> 00:04:57,803
With the layout in place, the inner pages become content templates.

64
00:04:57,803 --> 00:05:01,938
For each content type, add a file to the Views folder whose name

65
00:05:01,938 --> 00:05:04,360
says which content item it renders.

66
00:05:05,110 --> 00:05:09,776
A hyphen separates the shape name, Content, from the content type.

67
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:15,349
A suffix after the last dot names a display type, so Content-BlogPost.Summary is

68
00:05:15,349 --> 00:05:18,070
a blog post as it appears in a list.

69
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:23,683
Copy the matching markup from the template into the file, then replace the

70
00:05:23,683 --> 00:05:26,843
sample text with the data of the content item.

71
00:05:26,843 --> 00:05:32,070
Here, the title reads DisplayText, and the subtitle is a field of the blog post.

72
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:36,447
A content item's parts and fields have shapes of their own.

73
00:05:36,447 --> 00:05:41,357
Model.Content holds them, and shape_render writes one, such as the HTML body part,

74
00:05:41,357 --> 00:05:43,310
wherever the markup needs it.

75
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:49,395
A placement.json file at the root of the theme decides which shapes render, and where.

76
00:05:49,395 --> 00:05:53,280
This rule hides the shape of the title part on the front end.

77
00:05:54,030 --> 00:05:59,502
The Templates reference lists the template names for content, widgets, parts, and fields,

78
00:05:59,502 --> 00:06:02,267
and the properties each template receives.

79
00:06:02,267 --> 00:06:05,550
The Views folder of TheBlogTheme shows them in use.

80
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:14,199
If the theme is meant to be reused, add a recipe to its Recipes folder.

81
00:06:14,199 --> 00:06:18,878
The blog recipe of TheBlogTheme enables the theme, selects it in the themes

82
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:21,940
step, and lists the zones in the settings step.

83
00:06:22,690 --> 00:06:27,130
Its other steps create the content types, menu, widgets, and layers.

84
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:31,930
Because issetuprecipe is true, the recipe is listed in the Recipe field of

85
00:06:31,930 --> 00:06:36,370
the setup screen, and choosing it sets up the site with all of this.

86
00:06:40,667 --> 00:06:44,602
A theme that the site references is listed under Design, Themes.

87
00:06:44,602 --> 00:06:48,761
Make Current selects it, and the card of the current site theme says

88
00:06:48,761 --> 00:06:50,840
This is the current Site theme.

89
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:52,807
Here, that is The Blog Theme.

90
00:06:53,481 --> 00:06:57,147
This is the front end of a site set up with the blog recipe.

91
00:06:57,147 --> 00:06:59,425
The design of the template is kept:

92
00:06:59,425 --> 00:07:03,313
the header image, the navigation, the post list, and the footer.

93
00:07:03,313 --> 00:07:07,591
The text comes from the site settings, the menu, and the content items.

94
00:07:08,198 --> 00:07:11,424
Opening a post shows the content template at work.

95
00:07:11,424 --> 00:07:15,974
The masthead holds the title, subtitle, author, and date, and the body of

96
00:07:15,974 --> 00:07:17,818
the post renders below it.

97
00:07:19,418 --> 00:07:20,318
To recap:

98
00:07:20,318 --> 00:07:25,063
copy the assets and declare them as resources, convert the main page into

99
00:07:25,063 --> 00:07:31,008
a layout, convert the inner pages into content templates, and optionally ship a setup recipe.

100
00:07:33,008 --> 00:07:39,074
A static template becomes a theme through assets, resources, a layout, and content templates.

101
00:07:39,074 --> 00:07:40,668
Thanks for watching.

